-- title:
--   Descending a lift from T/𝔪^N when 𝔪^N=0
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \neq 2$ and a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and let $E_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ whose formal group satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. relative to the ideal $\bot$ the $q$-th series of $E_0$'s formal group is a unit multiple of the Drinfeld divisor `drinfeldDivisor q 0 0`. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with maximal ideal generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is that maximal ideal. Let $T$ be an Artinian local $W_0$-algebra with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ whose kernel is $\mathfrak m_T$ and which agrees with $\mathrm{res}_0$ on the image of $W_0$, let $G$ be a commutative formal group law over $T$ obtained from the formal group of $E_0$ by base change along $\mathrm{res}_T$ (its defining two-variable series is the image of that of $E_0$ under `MvPowerSeries.map resT`), and let $N$ satisfy $\mathfrak m_T^N = \bot$. Assume there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ with $E$ reducing to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, a formal group $G_n$ over $T/\mathfrak m_T^N$ whose series is the fixed formal group law `formalGroupLawFixed` of the reduction of $E$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^N$, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi$ from $G_n$ to the reduction of $G$ modulo $\mathfrak m_T^N$ (a power series with zero constant term, satisfying the homomorphism identity and with unit linear coefficient) such that every coefficient of $\psi$'s series differs from the corresponding coefficient of $X$ by an element of the image of $\mathfrak m_T$ in $T/\mathfrak m_T^N$. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $E$ over $T$ reducing to $E_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, a formal group $G'$ over $T$ whose series is $E$'s `formalGroupLawFixed`, and an isomorphism of formal group laws $\psi : G' \to G$ all of whose coefficients satisfy $\mathrm{res}_T(\mathrm{coeff}_n \psi) = \delta_{n,1}$.
--
--   This is the closing step of the existence half of the Serre–Tate theory of local moduli for the formal group of an elliptic curve over an Artinian local ring: once the nilpotency index of $\mathfrak m_T$ has been exhausted in the induction through small extensions, a lift matching modulo $\mathfrak m_T^N$ is a lift over $T$ itself. It feeds the assembly [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_map_eq_and_lawIso_of_isBaseChange_formalGroup_of_isArtinianRing).
